# {name}

This is a Lembic notebook project. A browser-based notebook UI is
watching this directory for changes.

## Structure
- `notebook.yaml` — Notebook manifest (cell order + metadata)
- `cells/` — One Python/Markdown file per cell
- `lib/` — Reusable function library (importable from cells)
- `outputs/` — Saved plots and tables
- `execution_log.jsonl` — Execution history

## Cell management

Create a cell (file + manifest in one step):
```
lembic add-cell [--type code|markdown] [--name NAME] [--after CELL_ID] [--content "..."]
```

Delete a cell:
```
lembic delete-cell CELL_ID
```

Move a cell:
```
lembic move-cell CELL_ID --after OTHER_ID
lembic move-cell CELL_ID --to-start
```

## Running cells
```
lembic run-cell CELL_ID
```
Executes a cell headlessly. Prints stdout, return values, and errors.

## Cell annotations

Leave visible notes on cells that appear as coloured banners in the UI.
Use annotations to communicate with the user — they persist in the
notebook and are visible even when the terminal is not in focus.

```
lembic annotate CELL_ID 'Annotation text' --style info|warning|success|error
lembic annotate CELL_ID --clear
```

When to annotate:
- After fixing a cell: explain what changed (`--style success`)
- Flagging a problem you cannot resolve: stale dependencies, missing
  data, ambiguous logic (`--style warning`)
- Execution errors with context: summarise the error and suggest a fix
  (`--style error`)
- General observations: performance notes, review comments (`--style info`)

## Notebook status
```
lembic status
```
Shows all cells with execution state and warnings.

## Kernel variables
```
lembic variables [--port 8000]
```
Shows current kernel variables (requires running server).

## Cell identifiers

CELL_ID in all commands above accepts any of:
- Full 8-char hex ID (e.g. `b739a1c2`)
- Short 4-char prefix shown in the UI (e.g. `b739`)
- Cell name (e.g. `odd-numbers`)

## Editing cells
- Edit cell files directly; the notebook watches for changes and
  updates the UI automatically.
- Cell order in the notebook matches the order in `notebook.yaml`.

## Git
- Do NOT add `Co-Authored-By` lines to commit messages.
